00:03:05.035 --> 00:03:08.075
Town's fiscal year twenty twenty five audit.

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:13.035
This evening, I will go over really the scope of work, the audit reports that were issued,

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.290
provide some overall financial and

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:22.330
then I will make our required communications. And again, happy to answer any questions that the Board members may have.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:30.965
As far as the scope of work, again, no changes from what has been done in prior years. We did do an audit of the town's financial statements.

00:03:31.205 --> 00:03:41.445
We performed that audit in accordance with both the auditing standards issued by the American Institute of Certified Public Accounts as well as the government auditing standards issued by the Government Accountability Office.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:50.400
In addition, based on the level of federal and state funding that was received and expended by the town, we did perform both federal and state single audits.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.000
In addition, we also performed an agreed upon procedures

00:03:54.080 --> 00:04:02.085
on the end of year school reports that are required to be filed with the State of Connecticut Department of Education.

00:04:02.885 --> 00:04:03.445
In

00:04:03.685 --> 00:04:08.005
addition to those attest services, we do perform some non audit services for the town.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:14.550
So again, we assist in the preparation of the financial statements as well as the schedule of expenditures of federal awards

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:17.910
and state financial assistance and then the related notes.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:22.150
We also assist in converting the town's governmental fund financial statements

00:04:22.805 --> 00:04:25.125
to the government wide financial statements.

00:04:25.605 --> 00:04:30.885
Although we do assist in these non audit services, again, are the responsibility of management.

00:04:31.285 --> 00:04:34.565
Management is responsible for the fair preparation

00:04:34.565 --> 00:04:35.765
of the financial statements,

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.910
the schedules of expenditures of federal awards and state financial assistance.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:44.070
Again, it is our responsibility to perform our audit procedures and

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.830
express an opinion

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.030
on those schedules.

00:04:49.205 --> 00:04:52.805
In connection with the audit, we do issue a number of reports.

00:04:53.045 --> 00:04:58.485
In terms of the report on the financial statements, we did issue unmodified clean opinions.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:05.830
Again, an unmodified opinion is expressed when we have concluded that the financial statements are fairly presented

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:10.470
in accordance with accounting principles generally accepted in The United States Of America.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.910
I do like to point out, if you read our opinion,

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:20.385
we do provide reasonable assurance that the financial statements are free from a material misstatement

00:05:20.465 --> 00:05:22.545
whether due to error or fraud.

00:05:22.785 --> 00:05:26.945
So again, we are providing reasonable assurance, not absolute assurance.

00:05:27.185 --> 00:05:29.185
We do not test every transaction.

00:05:29.505 --> 00:05:32.065
We do rely on some representations from management.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.720
There are estimates included in the financial statements,

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.440
and therefore, we cannot provide absolute assurance.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:42.040
But again, reasonable assurance is still a very high level of assurance.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.280
In addition to the financial statement

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:52.395
report, we also issue a report on compliance and on internal control over financial reporting.

00:05:52.715 --> 00:05:57.195
If you read through this report, we do not actually express an opinion

00:05:57.435 --> 00:06:00.955
on the town's compliance with laws and regulations

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.580
or on the effectiveness of the town's internal controls.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:05.700
Essentially,

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.980
during the course of performing the financial statement and compliance audits,

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.100
if we

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.580
identify either a material noncompliance

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:13.780
with laws and regulations

00:06:14.405 --> 00:06:21.925
or a material weakness or significant deficiency in the town's internal controls, we are required to communicate it in this letter.

00:06:23.125 --> 00:06:28.565
Again, just as a follow-up in the prior year, we did have three findings that we reported in this letter.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:34.740
We had a material weakness in internal control over financial reporting related to the reconciliation

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:38.020
of the towns and school districts general ledgers.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:42.020
We have repeated this finding as a material weakness

00:06:42.205 --> 00:06:47.565
in internal control over the current year as well, and I will discuss that a little bit more on the next slide.

00:06:48.285 --> 00:06:56.660
In the prior year, we also issued a significant deficiency in internal control over financial reporting related to the bank and interfund reconciliations

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.260
at the school district.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:03.540
Again, to report that we are no longer reporting that as a significant

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:06.500
deficiency in internal control over financial reporting.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.580
So again, that finding has not been repeated.

00:07:09.545 --> 00:07:11.305
And then we did issue a

00:07:11.465 --> 00:07:14.425
prior year finding, an instance of non compliance

00:07:15.065 --> 00:07:19.065
related to some reporting on the ARPA funds.

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:22.745
Again, we were not required to test that program in the current year.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.500
It was our understanding that that report was filed timely, and therefore we have not

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.540
repeated that as an instance of noncompliance

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:31.820
in the current year.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.820
So again, our report on internal control

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:41.675
in the current year had one finding reported, which we considered to be a material weakness.

00:07:41.915 --> 00:07:43.995
Again, that related to the reconciliation

00:07:43.995 --> 00:07:47.835
between the school district's general ledger and the town's general ledger.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.450
Again, those ledgers are not currently integrated.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:56.810
Journal entries are required to record and reconcile the activity of the school district with the town.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:02.970
The town's year end closing process to record the school district's balance and activities were ultimately incomplete.

00:08:03.565 --> 00:08:09.405
We did have some material audit adjustments that were proposed to record and reconcile that activity.

00:08:09.965 --> 00:08:15.165
Ultimately, made the recommendation that the town no longer records balances

00:08:15.165 --> 00:08:18.765
and activities that are already accounted for by the school district.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.350
So again,

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:27.950
activity that's already recorded in the school district's general ledger does not have to be duplicated in the town's accounting records.

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:35.065
The town should ultimately limit its accounting to transactions that involve direct financial activity between the town and the school district.

00:08:35.385 --> 00:08:37.065
That would include appropriations,

00:08:37.065 --> 00:08:40.105
transfers, reimbursements, or shared service costs.

00:08:40.585 --> 00:08:45.385
In addition, we recommended that the school district continue to provide the town with its monthly financial reports

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:50.070
to ensure that the town remains informed of the school district's fiscal status.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:55.670
So again, management is required to address these findings through a corrective action plan.

00:08:56.150 --> 00:09:01.270
That plan was actually, completed and filed with the, state

00:09:00.385 --> 00:09:02.225
office of policy and management.

00:09:05.505 --> 00:09:06.945
In connection with the audit,

00:09:07.185 --> 00:09:10.945
we do a federal single audit and we issue a report on compliance

00:09:11.025 --> 00:09:13.505
on internal control at the federal award level.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:19.550
In this report, we do actually express an opinion on the town's compliance with its major federal

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.350
programs.

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:22.350
For fiscal year 2025,

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:25.630
the total federal awards that were expended was just over 1,000,000.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:29.150
The major program was the highway planning and construction grant.

00:09:30.015 --> 00:09:32.575
I believe that was for the Bunker Hill Bridge

00:09:33.375 --> 00:09:34.255
replacement.

00:09:34.415 --> 00:09:37.375
We did issue unmodified clean opinions on compliance,

00:09:37.615 --> 00:09:42.175
and we did not report any significant deficiencies or material weaknesses over grant compliance.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:44.500
Issue a Mike, can

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:51.860
>> ask you a question, if you don't mind? Because so I don't forget. Can you can you explain what

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:54.820
what is meant by a single audit

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:58.225
>> versus Sure. So yep. There are

00:09:59.185 --> 00:10:01.745
different levels of audits that are required.

00:10:02.865 --> 00:10:07.825
And under the federal guidelines and the state guidelines, if you expend over a certain

00:10:08.065 --> 00:10:14.110
dollar of federal awards or state financial assistance, you are required to undergo a compliance audit.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:20.190
And so for that audit, we perform additional procedures to determine that you are complying with the requirements

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:21.950
of your major programs.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:28.635
So again, there is a whole set of standards that we have to follow in terms of doing a compliance audit.

00:10:30.315 --> 00:10:30.795
So

00:10:32.555 --> 00:10:36.555
>> it an additional level of audit above and beyond the financial statement audit.

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:37.930
Okay.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:40.090
Alright. Thank you. Yep.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:50.810
>> So again, we do we issue a similar reporting connection with the state single audit. For fiscal year twenty twenty five, the total state financial assistance that was expended was about 2,800,000

00:10:51.675 --> 00:10:54.235
The major programs was the local bridge

00:10:54.475 --> 00:10:55.835
transportation fund,

00:10:56.075 --> 00:11:04.715
and then the town aid road grants. Again, we did issue unmodified clean opinions on compliance, and we did not report any significant deficiencies or material weaknesses over compliance.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.080
So in general,

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:09.640
again, clean from a compliance perspective,

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:16.680
