This slide covers your general fund budgetary highlights. So your original and final budgets did provide for the use of fund balance of approximately $79,000

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:39.030
Your actual change in fund balance was an increase of about $302,000

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:43.670
so that did result in an overall favorable budgetary variance of about 382,000

00:11:44.745 --> 00:11:48.585
The surplus was driven by revenues and other financings,

00:11:49.465 --> 00:11:51.225
which were about $166,000

00:11:51.225 --> 00:11:52.265
more than budgeted.

00:11:52.425 --> 00:11:56.585
You had favorable collections on property taxes and interest on short term investments.

00:11:57.030 --> 00:12:00.630
And then overall, your actual expenditures were about $216,000

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:01.910
less than budgeted.

