00:13:56.440 --> 00:14:00.200
Again, those amounts are either restricted or committed for various purposes.

00:14:00.695 --> 00:14:06.535
And again, a very trivial deficit in the historic preservation fund. Again, just bring that to your attention

00:14:06.775 --> 00:14:08.295
as, you know, ultimately

00:14:08.775 --> 00:14:11.975
no governmental funds should have a deficit fund balance.

00:14:12.295 --> 00:14:14.535
Again, these aren't significant and ultimately should be,

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:19.230
funded by the general fund or some other sources.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:25.710
All right. And then the last section just includes our required communications.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:38.485
The first item here talks about our responsibility under the auditing standards. So as I mentioned before, management is responsible for the financial statements. It's our responsibility to express our opinions on those financial statements.

00:14:39.125 --> 00:14:44.485
In terms of the plan scope and timing of audit, again, no changes in the overall scope of work that was performed.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:49.180
There were four one month extensions that were obtained from OPM.

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:56.380
Those delays were attributed to delays in commencement of the audit field work really due to scheduling constraints.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:15:00.460
I do want to make mention in terms of municipal auditors.

00:15:01.745 --> 00:15:02.545
There's

00:15:03.505 --> 00:15:07.745
definitely a lack of capacity for that type of expertise.

00:15:09.025 --> 00:15:13.265
You know, out of the 169 municipalities that do file their audit,

00:15:13.665 --> 00:15:15.825
over half of them file them on extension.

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:25.820
So again, I think probably last year, only 40 municipalities were able to file their audit reports on time. So part of the delays is, yes, we start the audit fieldwork in December.

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:29.420
Our hopes is typically to get that done by the end of February,

00:15:30.885 --> 00:15:36.485
except there were some additional delays related really to the transition of town finance personnel.

00:15:37.845 --> 00:15:40.165
In terms of significant audit findings, again,

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:52.940
typically highlight whether or not there is any new accounting standards that impacted the financial statements. Again, were no new accounting standards that were implemented in FY 2025 that had a significant effect on the financial statements.

00:15:55.035 --> 00:16:00.235
Do you need to disclose that the financial statements do include some significant estimates and judgments?

00:16:00.555 --> 00:16:04.235
Those consisted of estimated useful lives that are assigned to capital assets,

00:16:04.795 --> 00:16:08.235
the discount rates utilized to determine your net pension and OPEB liabilities,

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.420
those are really at the state level,

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:15.620
and then estimated amounts of vacation and sick leave to be used in future years.

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:19.060
We did review those estimates, and we did deem them to be reasonable,

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:20.260
with industry

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:21.140
practices.

00:16:22.625 --> 00:16:27.345
Happy to report that there were no significant difficulties encountered in performing the audits

00:16:27.745 --> 00:16:29.905
other than some of those transition issues.

00:16:30.465 --> 00:16:35.345
We did issue a separate management letter containing some other audit recommendations.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:47.660
However, we're not required to specifically communicate those to the Board. I did want to make you aware of them that there's a separate management letter that we did issue, and we'll follow-up with those recommendations during the next audit.

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.460
Were no uncorrected misstatements.

